1
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:05,872
GETAWAY AND GO WITH JANGDOBARI

2
00:00:05,939 --> 00:00:07,907
I shouldn't get too excited.
Need to calm down.

3
00:00:07,974 --> 00:00:09,776
One, two, three, four.

4
00:00:10,276 --> 00:00:11,411
JANG DO-YEON

5
00:00:11,478 --> 00:00:12,746
I need to snap out of it.

6
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:13,813
This is work.

7
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:16,816
THE THINGS THAT LIE AHEAD OF HER…

8
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:19,819
SOME BUTTERFLIES…

9
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:20,887
You're Tang Wei now.

10
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:22,856
Did I make you blush today?

11
00:00:22,922 --> 00:00:24,290
Me? Of course you did.

12
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:25,625
Honey?

13
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:27,027
Honey.

14
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:28,828
We're close to Russia, so…

15
00:00:28,895 --> 00:00:32,699
SOME MOMENTS OF JOY

16
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:35,001
AND SOME MOMENTS OF SHOCK

17
00:00:35,068 --> 00:00:37,637
Thank you for giving me
such unforgettable memories.

18
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:39,305
LET'S BEGIN THIS UNFORGETTABLE STORY

19
00:00:39,839 --> 00:00:40,874
HARBIN AIRPORT

20
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:43,576
That was fast. I thought
we'd have to wait for it to arrive.

21
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,179
-Taxi!
-Shall we get on the one behind?

22
00:00:48,448 --> 00:00:51,351
BARIBARI

23
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,960
WHERE ARE WE HEADED
WITH BARIBARI BUNDLES OF STUFF?

24
00:01:01,027 --> 00:01:02,695
Ever since I heard

25
00:01:03,663 --> 00:01:07,834
that we would be going to Harbin,

26
00:01:08,334 --> 00:01:10,503
I've been studying
some basic Mandarin phrases

27
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:13,039
that even elementary students
would understand.

28
00:01:13,106 --> 00:01:15,575
Zao shang hao.
A morning greeting. "Hello."

29
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:18,044
Xiao hao. An afternoon greeting. "Hello."

30
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:21,381
Wan shang hao.
A greeting for the evening. "Hello."

31
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:22,348
Wan an.

32
00:01:22,849 --> 00:01:23,850
Good night.

33
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,618
Wo yao pijiu.

34
00:01:25,685 --> 00:01:26,786
I'd like beer, please.

35
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,222
DO-YEON IS A BEER LOVER

36
00:01:29,789 --> 00:01:31,057
You took notes too?

37
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:32,192
"Cheers."

38
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:36,796
What are you most looking forward to
on this trip?

39
00:01:36,863 --> 00:01:38,364
Looking forward to? The food.

40
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:40,867
A refreshing beer and some tasty snacks.

41
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,203
Love that sort of thing.

42
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,571
It's so delicious.

43
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:47,540
How do you feel now we're here?
Are you excited?

44
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:48,708
I had a lightbulb moment

45
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:51,578
that it's been a good while
since I've had an outdoor shoot.

46
00:01:51,644 --> 00:01:52,479
Once we landed,

47
00:01:53,179 --> 00:01:54,347
I saw myself at the airport,

48
00:01:54,414 --> 00:01:57,217
and I was so studio-ready
with a full face of makeup.

49
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,352
I took a glance at my travel buddy,

50
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:01,955
and they came totally on theme
for a chill holiday,

51
00:02:02,021 --> 00:02:03,790
so I felt so embarrassed.

52
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:06,126
As soon as I got to a bathroom,
I removed my falsies.

53
00:02:06,192 --> 00:02:07,293
My lashes were like this.

54
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,962
"Hello."

55
00:02:09,028 --> 00:02:09,929
They were so…

56
00:02:10,497 --> 00:02:13,533
They were a little too outspoken,
so I removed them

57
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,301
and returned to my natural state.

58
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:19,205
I'm still getting used to things,
but I'm sure that with time,

59
00:02:19,272 --> 00:02:21,174
I'll loosen up a little for our viewers.

60
00:02:21,241 --> 00:02:22,375
LET'S SEE IF THAT HAPPENS

61
00:02:22,442 --> 00:02:23,476
I believe so.

62
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:27,514
What are you filming?

63
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,815
GETAWAY AND GO WITH JANGDOBARI

64
00:02:29,716 --> 00:02:32,418
EPISODE 1: HARBIN COUPLE'S HOLIDAY
WE GOT MARRIED

65
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:39,626
Hello. Bound for a breezy break
with bundles of stories in my bag.

66
00:02:39,692 --> 00:02:41,694
I'm Jang Do-yeon
of Getaway and Go with Jangdobari.

67
00:02:41,761 --> 00:02:42,595
JANG DO-YEON

68
00:02:43,363 --> 00:02:45,498
CHEERS ALL AROUND

69
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:46,866
Everyone,

70
00:02:47,901 --> 00:02:48,735
do you see this?

71
00:02:48,801 --> 00:02:51,504
I'm no longer in Korea but in Harbin.

72
00:02:52,772 --> 00:02:55,508
I've brought a lot of stuff,

73
00:02:55,575 --> 00:02:58,778
but I won't be traveling alone
as I have a travel buddy.

74
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:02,448
This show is all about unloading
bundles of stories

75
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:05,385
and having fun with some travel buddies.

76
00:03:05,451 --> 00:03:07,120
Shall we meet our buddy?

77
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:11,457
A SUSPICIOUS FIGURE IS WATCHING

78
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:14,694
If I'm to give you a clue
about this buddy of ours,

79
00:03:15,295 --> 00:03:18,531
I can't remember a time
when this person hasn't been popular.

80
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:19,432
GLARING

81
00:03:19,499 --> 00:03:21,568
They've always been in their prime.

82
00:03:21,634 --> 00:03:24,504
And we've met before,
so we're not complete strangers,

83
00:03:24,571 --> 00:03:25,805
but we're not that close,

84
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:27,373
nor are we uncomfortable.

85
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:31,077
I'm actually quite amused
that this person willingly volunteered

86
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:32,712
to join me on this show.

87
00:03:32,779 --> 00:03:34,247
If I tell my friends

88
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:36,616
that this person is my first travel buddy,

89
00:03:36,683 --> 00:03:39,252
I think a lot of them would be jealous.

90
00:03:39,319 --> 00:03:40,653
-Hello.
-And I--

91
00:03:42,121 --> 00:03:43,590
It's Byun Yo-han.

92
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:47,060
LOTS TO UNPACK

93
00:03:47,126 --> 00:03:48,528
STRUGGLING

94
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,129
It's good to see you.

95
00:03:51,097 --> 00:03:52,031
How have you been?

96
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:55,268
BYUN YO-HAN
ACTOR

97
00:03:55,335 --> 00:03:57,470
I'm such a fan,
so I really wanted to meet you.

98
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:02,008
THE TWO PREVIOUSLY MET
A YEAR AGO ON SALON DRIP

99
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,743
I don't usually say this sort of thing,

100
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:04,777
but are you in a mood?

101
00:04:04,844 --> 00:04:05,678
MOODY CHARM

102
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,447
I am a moody guy. Okay, cheers.

103
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:09,115
WILL PROUDLY TOAST HIMSELF

104
00:04:09,182 --> 00:04:11,417
HE SHOWED ALL

105
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:13,086
OF HIS MULTI-FACETED CHARM

106
00:04:13,152 --> 00:04:14,087
Did I drool just now?

107
00:04:14,153 --> 00:04:15,922
You're an indescribable character.

108
00:04:15,989 --> 00:04:17,490
A NEW TYPE OF CHEMISTRY

109
00:04:17,991 --> 00:04:20,093
TWO HOURS AGO

110
00:04:20,159 --> 00:04:21,694
It still smells the same.

111
00:04:22,562 --> 00:04:23,730
It's this smell.

112
00:04:23,796 --> 00:04:24,631
WHIFF

113
00:04:25,131 --> 00:04:25,965
Sir?

114
00:04:26,866 --> 00:04:29,535
I was a student studying abroad here

115
00:04:30,036 --> 00:04:31,638
about 17 years ago.

116
00:04:32,505 --> 00:04:33,339
STORY BUNDLE 1

117
00:04:33,406 --> 00:04:36,109
YO-HAN DID A TWO-YEAR LANGUAGE EXCHANGE
IN HARBIN AT THE AGE OF 20

118
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:38,044
I'm in Harbin again.

119
00:04:38,911 --> 00:04:40,179
It feels surreal.

120
00:04:41,014 --> 00:04:41,914
A lot has changed.

121
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:44,917
I had this older friend
called Kang Min-cheol

122
00:04:44,984 --> 00:04:47,453
who was studying Chinese Literature
at Korea University.

123
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,122
I learned from him for about three years.

124
00:04:49,188 --> 00:04:50,023
STORY BUNDLE 2

125
00:04:50,089 --> 00:04:51,924
MIN-CHEOL TAUGHT HIM CHINESE
IN HIGH SCHOOL

126
00:04:51,991 --> 00:04:52,825
Wow.

127
00:04:53,926 --> 00:04:55,295
So much has changed.

128
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,096
There was none of this back then.

129
00:04:57,163 --> 00:04:58,665
STORY BUNDLE 3
HARBIN LOOKS SO DIFFERENT

130
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:04,771
Should I go out now?

131
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:07,507
SHOULDER BUMPS THE AUTOMATIC DOORS

132
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,742
SHY REUNION IN A YEAR

133
00:05:09,809 --> 00:05:11,010
This isn't a prank show.

134
00:05:11,077 --> 00:05:12,178
-Exactly.
-Honestly.

135
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:14,113
-I just came here as I was told.
-Yes?

136
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:17,283
But I didn't think I'd be back in Harbin.

137
00:05:17,350 --> 00:05:22,221
I thought maybe I'd come back with my wife
in the future, when I'm married.

138
00:05:22,722 --> 00:05:24,524
Then should we hurry to find a venue?

139
00:05:25,024 --> 00:05:26,492
FLASH PROPOSAL

140
00:05:26,559 --> 00:05:28,695
We could get a divorce three days later.

141
00:05:28,761 --> 00:05:29,696
That sounds good.

142
00:05:29,762 --> 00:05:32,031
-But no physical touch.
-Like a married couple.

143
00:05:32,098 --> 00:05:33,166
I wanted to see you.

144
00:05:33,232 --> 00:05:34,400
-You did?
-Yes.

145
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:36,636
But seeing you in Harbin
makes this even more special.

146
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:37,537
Right.

147
00:05:37,603 --> 00:05:38,838
Earlier in the airport,

148
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:41,274
you didn't seem to know your way around.

149
00:05:41,341 --> 00:05:43,609
THE PAIR WERE ON THE SAME PLANE OVER

150
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:45,278
You did study in Harbin, didn't you?

151
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,379
Of course I did.

152
00:05:46,446 --> 00:05:47,280
SPACING OUT

153
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:48,247
Let's head inside.

154
00:05:49,048 --> 00:05:50,116
I'll carry this for you.

155
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,051
-I've got it.
-Seriously?

156
00:05:52,118 --> 00:05:53,786
-Hang on.
-It's quite heavy, isn't it?

157
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:55,388
You're too kind.

158
00:05:55,455 --> 00:05:56,289
HUBBY TAKES CHARGE

159
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:58,891
The least I can do
is open the door for you.

160
00:05:58,958 --> 00:06:00,827
Deary me.

161
00:06:03,162 --> 00:06:03,996
Hello.

162
00:06:05,932 --> 00:06:06,999
-Your passport.
-Sure.

163
00:06:08,334 --> 00:06:10,236
People would think we're sharing a room.

164
00:06:10,737 --> 00:06:12,271
I was only joking.

165
00:06:12,338 --> 00:06:13,172
Of course.

166
00:06:14,307 --> 00:06:15,908
-Would that be okay?
-Sure, fine.

167
00:06:16,509 --> 00:06:17,377
I'm good too.

168
00:06:17,443 --> 00:06:18,511
Me too.

169
00:06:18,578 --> 00:06:20,012
The bathroom might be an issue.

170
00:06:20,079 --> 00:06:22,081
We could blast music, though.

171
00:06:22,982 --> 00:06:25,284
Wait, you know that trick? Blasting music.

172
00:06:25,351 --> 00:06:26,185
Of course I do.

173
00:06:26,252 --> 00:06:27,320
I'll leave the tap running.

174
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,221
ALREADY IN SYNC

175
00:06:28,287 --> 00:06:29,222
Let's go.

176
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:31,524
This is great.

177
00:06:31,591 --> 00:06:33,726
Please, Yo-han. I can take my own trunk.

178
00:06:35,361 --> 00:06:36,529
This is hilarious.

179
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:38,998
ALL CHECKED IN TO SEPARATE ROOMS

180
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:42,001
TEEHEE

181
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:44,504
Now you've changed,
you're like a different person.

182
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,406
Well, talk about pot calling kettle black.

183
00:06:46,472 --> 00:06:49,142
"Pot calling kettle black"?
Haven't heard that in a while.

184
00:06:49,809 --> 00:06:51,110
-Get in.
-After you.

185
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:53,112
CONSIDERATE COUPLE

186
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,252
Look at this angle.

187
00:06:59,318 --> 00:07:00,887
Isn't this angle like the one

188
00:07:00,953 --> 00:07:03,022
from Director Park Chan-wook's movie?

189
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:04,457
-Decision to Leave?
-Yes.

190
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:08,394
Dead or alive, we stick together.

191
00:07:08,461 --> 00:07:09,362
Of course.

192
00:07:10,997 --> 00:07:12,031
Let's speak comfortably.

193
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,099
-Me to you?
-Yes.

194
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,234
What should I call you?

195
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:16,669
-Call me?
-Yes.

196
00:07:16,736 --> 00:07:17,570
Nuna?

197
00:07:19,572 --> 00:07:20,840
You can call me Tang Wei.

198
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,645
We're Korean,
so you can call me Gamja-Tang Wei.

199
00:07:25,711 --> 00:07:26,779
Well, I think…

200
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,548
I should be Park Kale.

201
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:31,083
-Well, kale is good for you.
-It is.

202
00:07:31,150 --> 00:07:32,919
And I'll be Gamja-Tang Wei.

203
00:07:33,653 --> 00:07:36,756
Have you already made
the decision to leave me?

204
00:07:38,191 --> 00:07:39,792
You've seen that movie?

205
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:41,561
I've even seen Following.

206
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:44,530
Following did well thanks to Salon Drip.

207
00:07:44,597 --> 00:07:45,798
Come on, that's not true.

208
00:07:45,865 --> 00:07:47,767
I honestly believe that.

209
00:07:47,834 --> 00:07:49,502
-You do?
-Honestly.

210
00:07:49,569 --> 00:07:52,338
When your new film comes out,
I'll make sure to check it out.

211
00:07:54,774 --> 00:07:55,942
What's it called again?

212
00:07:57,276 --> 00:07:58,411
Your World.

213
00:08:00,713 --> 00:08:02,648
-Directed by Yi Ok-seop.
-Your World.

214
00:08:02,715 --> 00:08:04,383
And starring actor Koo Kyo-hwan.

215
00:08:04,884 --> 00:08:06,986
When I saw the stills

216
00:08:07,053 --> 00:08:12,158
of these two charming people
gazing into each other's eyes,

217
00:08:12,225 --> 00:08:13,926
I was totally drawn in.

218
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:15,094
Really?

219
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,796
I could feel your energies.

220
00:08:16,863 --> 00:08:20,233
A still cut gives you
a taste of what it was like on set.

221
00:08:20,733 --> 00:08:23,536
Just by looking at those stills,
I was intrigued by the film.

222
00:08:23,603 --> 00:08:24,437
You were?

223
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,239
I think the film will be fascinating.

224
00:08:26,739 --> 00:08:28,474
I'm fascinated that I'm even in a film.

225
00:08:28,975 --> 00:08:31,244
The Mandarin phrases
you practiced earlier…

226
00:08:31,744 --> 00:08:33,279
-What were they?
-Show him.

227
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:34,914
I'd like a beer.

228
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:36,949
That's a lovely phrase.

229
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,518
MOST CONFIDENT AT ORDERING BEER

230
00:08:38,584 --> 00:08:39,685
That's spot on.

231
00:08:39,752 --> 00:08:42,822
Just say that every day
until we leave Harbin.

232
00:08:42,889 --> 00:08:43,956
I'D LIKE BEER, PLEASE

233
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,225
So, for our first destination…

234
00:08:46,292 --> 00:08:48,861
I didn't ask, but we're getting dumplings.
My favorite.

235
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,396
ZHANG BAO PU

236
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:53,633
A DUMPLING JOINT IN HARBIN
WITH OVER A CENTURY'S HISTORY

237
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:05,545
-Oh boy.
-Boy.

238
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,748
So it's here?

239
00:09:08,814 --> 00:09:12,218
For the sake of smooth travels,
shall we drop the honorifics?

240
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:14,787
Sounds good. I love it.

241
00:09:15,454 --> 00:09:16,756
Yes, right. This is great.

242
00:09:18,624 --> 00:09:20,760
It says it's a century old.

243
00:09:21,627 --> 00:09:23,162
Yeah, it says "1902" here.

244
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,397
OPEN SINCE 1902

245
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,433
Are there seats?

246
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:28,801
Seats?

247
00:09:28,868 --> 00:09:31,170
It's packed full of people.

248
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:33,472
They want us to go upstairs.

249
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:34,974
Thank you.

250
00:09:35,541 --> 00:09:36,509
That looks delicious.

251
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,012
Are you allowed to drink?

252
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:40,913
Can you?

253
00:09:41,681 --> 00:09:42,548
Would that be okay?

254
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:45,318
-Shall we pick up the honorifics again?
-Oh, I don't know.

255
00:09:46,619 --> 00:09:49,188
-There's a breeze. Will you keep that on?
-Yes, I'm good.

256
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,690
-Give me that.
-Such a gentleman.

257
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:51,657
You are my wife.

258
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,393
Thank you, Park Kale.

259
00:09:57,797 --> 00:10:00,166
I'm here at this famous joint
all thanks to you.

260
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,935
I was too broke to come as a student.

261
00:10:04,136 --> 00:10:05,705
I'll pay with Alipay.

262
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:06,672
I'm so grateful.

263
00:10:07,306 --> 00:10:08,341
I'll enjoy the meal.

264
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:10,309
Hello.

265
00:10:10,876 --> 00:10:12,878
This is the character for "bean,"
so it must be tofu.

266
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:13,779
-Gyoza.
-Tofu.

267
00:10:15,915 --> 00:10:16,916
ONE TOFU DUMPLING

268
00:10:16,983 --> 00:10:18,951
ONE SMALL RIB DUMPLING

269
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:21,420
I think it's this.

270
00:10:22,722 --> 00:10:23,556
ONE MAJIANG LIANGPI

271
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,257
I heard this one's delicious.

272
00:10:25,324 --> 00:10:26,692
If there's anything you want…

273
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:28,394
Meiyou… I mean, no, I don't.

274
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:30,196
You're speaking Mandarin to me now?

275
00:10:30,696 --> 00:10:33,199
Harbin is known for its beer.

276
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:34,900
-So let's go with Hapi.
-Great.

277
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:36,335
GO AHEAD

278
00:10:36,402 --> 00:10:37,269
First,

279
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:39,639
we'd like two beers, please.

280
00:10:40,406 --> 00:10:43,476
TWO BOTTLES OF HARBIN BEER

281
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:46,679
What type of traveler are you?

282
00:10:46,746 --> 00:10:49,081
-Do you travel alone or with friends?
-You first. You?

283
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:51,217
I used to prefer traveling alone,

284
00:10:51,283 --> 00:10:54,020
but I've found traveling with a friend
you click with is great.

285
00:10:54,086 --> 00:10:56,055
I like how we're doing it today.

286
00:10:56,756 --> 00:10:59,091
-The two of us.
-How exactly are we doing it today?

287
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:01,093
We locked eyes, then got married.

288
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,529
As soon as we checked in.

289
00:11:03,596 --> 00:11:04,430
I love it.

290
00:11:06,732 --> 00:11:07,600
Wow.

291
00:11:08,234 --> 00:11:09,068
Looks good.

292
00:11:09,135 --> 00:11:10,369
FIRST MENU
MAJIANG LIANGPI

293
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:11,904
KEEN EYES

294
00:11:13,072 --> 00:11:13,906
Is this Harbin…

295
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:16,542
I think it is Hapi, but let me check.

296
00:11:17,109 --> 00:11:18,978
-Is it what we're…
-No, this isn't it.

297
00:11:19,912 --> 00:11:21,247
Excuse me?

298
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:23,749
Do you not have Hapi?

299
00:11:23,816 --> 00:11:25,217
-We don't.
-You don't?

300
00:11:25,284 --> 00:11:26,118
Thank you.

301
00:11:27,086 --> 00:11:28,821
This is Xuehua,

302
00:11:28,888 --> 00:11:32,158
a Northeastern specialty beer, apparently.

303
00:11:32,224 --> 00:11:34,093
-It still looks good.
-I'll open it.

304
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,161
No Harbin beer?

305
00:11:35,227 --> 00:11:36,929
I did understand "meiyou."

306
00:11:36,996 --> 00:11:38,064
They don't have Hapi now.

307
00:11:38,564 --> 00:11:39,699
-Okay.
-You understood.

308
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:42,301
-I'll pour you a glass first.
-Thank you.

309
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,202
RESPECTFULLY

310
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:44,103
Damn it.

311
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:46,338
-You punk.
-I'm just joking.

312
00:11:46,405 --> 00:11:47,673
You're not that much younger.

313
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:49,041
-You know I'm joking, right?
-Yes.

314
00:11:49,108 --> 00:11:49,942
DO-YEON, BORN IN 1985

315
00:11:50,009 --> 00:11:51,477
BYUN YO-HAN, BORN IN 1986

316
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:52,611
ONLY A YEAR YOUNGER

317
00:11:52,678 --> 00:11:55,014
-You're coming to life now.
-No, I was just joking.

318
00:11:55,081 --> 00:11:56,782
I was kidding. You're my guest.

319
00:11:59,185 --> 00:12:00,086
Thank you.

320
00:12:00,619 --> 00:12:01,687
Thank you.

321
00:12:02,188 --> 00:12:04,757
CHUGGING THEIR FIRST BEERS

322
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:06,992
It's not bitter at all.

323
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,462
It tastes like barley.

324
00:12:09,528 --> 00:12:10,629
-Right.
-Isn't it great?

325
00:12:10,696 --> 00:12:12,231
Did you have beer like this back then?

326
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:14,667
-Back in school?
-Back then, I drank Hapi.

327
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:15,568
Harbin beer.

328
00:12:15,634 --> 00:12:16,869
-That's called Hapi?
-Yes.

329
00:12:16,936 --> 00:12:18,404
It was everywhere back then,

330
00:12:18,471 --> 00:12:20,106
so it's odd that they don't have any.

331
00:12:20,172 --> 00:12:21,373
Then tell me something.

332
00:12:21,941 --> 00:12:24,844
We have to hang out for the next two days.

333
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:27,079
Is there anything you don't want me to do?

334
00:12:27,146 --> 00:12:29,148
There's nothing of the sort.
We're here on a trip.

335
00:12:29,215 --> 00:12:30,182
Let's try everything.

336
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:31,283
Really?

337
00:12:31,350 --> 00:12:32,585
I'd like you to let loose.

338
00:12:32,651 --> 00:12:34,086
-I'll do the same.
-You will?

339
00:12:34,153 --> 00:12:35,387
I'll ask you a question, then.

340
00:12:35,454 --> 00:12:37,223
Any lines you don't want me to cross?

341
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:38,991
Any lines?

342
00:12:39,058 --> 00:12:40,526
I'm fine with almost everything.

343
00:12:41,026 --> 00:12:44,997
We'll be drinking a couple of glasses
of Harbin beer, right?

344
00:12:45,064 --> 00:12:47,633
You know when people ask, "Are you drunk?"

345
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,168
-You don't want me to say that?
-Yes.

346
00:12:49,235 --> 00:12:50,770
Things like "Are you drunk?"

347
00:12:50,836 --> 00:12:52,671
That must be one of your pet peeves.

348
00:12:52,738 --> 00:12:54,974
-It's a total buzzkill.
-I get you.

349
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:56,208
I agree with you.

350
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:57,243
You do?

351
00:12:57,309 --> 00:12:58,544
"You're drunk. Go home."

352
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,780
No saying things like,
"You should think about tomorrow."

353
00:13:00,846 --> 00:13:02,081
I hate that stuff too.

354
00:13:02,148 --> 00:13:02,982
Okay.

355
00:13:03,482 --> 00:13:05,017
Okay, cheers.

356
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:07,153
NO BUZZKILL TALK

357
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:10,289
MAJIANG LIANGPI

358
00:13:10,356 --> 00:13:15,161
TRANSLUCENT, WIDE NOODLES
TOSSED IN A COLD, REFRESHING PEANUT SAUCE

359
00:13:15,227 --> 00:13:16,796
-Shall we eat? Here.
-Yes.

360
00:13:17,863 --> 00:13:21,700
NEWLYWED CHEMISTRY OFF THE CHARTS

361
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:23,335
Let's mix it

362
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:24,804
together.

363
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,440
We're still a little cautious.

364
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:31,243
Wait, no being cautious.

365
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:33,312
HARBIN COUPLE'S TRAVEL RULES:
NO BEING CAUTIOUS

366
00:13:33,379 --> 00:13:34,280
While we're traveling.

367
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:35,614
I like it.

368
00:13:35,681 --> 00:13:36,816
Let's mix.

369
00:13:39,685 --> 00:13:40,519
Okay.

370
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,489
MIXING WITHOUT CAUTION

371
00:13:44,723 --> 00:13:45,891
It smells great.

372
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,228
FLINCH

373
00:13:49,295 --> 00:13:50,129
FLINCH22

374
00:13:50,196 --> 00:13:52,665
I'm sorry. I was cautious just now
with my chopsticks.

375
00:13:52,731 --> 00:13:54,300
Come on, we said no being cautious.

376
00:13:54,366 --> 00:13:56,902
I know we said that,
but it was just instinctive.

377
00:13:57,636 --> 00:13:58,838
Do you like spicy food?

378
00:13:58,904 --> 00:13:59,939
You don't?

379
00:14:00,005 --> 00:14:01,507
No, I do.

380
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:02,808
Then eat up.

381
00:14:05,911 --> 00:14:07,580
-Am I acting moody?
-No.

382
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:10,916
Why would you remember that?

383
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:12,251
I found it so funny.

384
00:14:12,318 --> 00:14:13,352
Are you in a mood?

385
00:14:13,419 --> 00:14:14,587
Then that's a relief.

386
00:14:14,653 --> 00:14:17,256
I also rather like that part
in a strange, perverted way.

387
00:14:19,425 --> 00:14:20,893
SLURP

388
00:14:25,598 --> 00:14:26,866
This just calls for some booze.

389
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:28,434
-It's so good.
-Right?

390
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:29,702
It's a total booze magnet.

391
00:14:29,768 --> 00:14:30,903
It's delicious.

392
00:14:32,137 --> 00:14:35,074
I thought it'd be like chewy rice cakes,
but it's super soft.

393
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:38,110
They're like flat glass noodles,
but a lot softer.

394
00:14:38,611 --> 00:14:39,445
They're good.

395
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:49,521
NEXT MENU
DUMPLINGS

396
00:14:49,588 --> 00:14:52,224
-This was so good.
-It was good.

397
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:53,692
EXPLAINING THE MENU

398
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,995
-Thank you.
-What did she say?

399
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:56,896
I have no clue.

400
00:14:58,397 --> 00:14:59,698
Have a taste.

401
00:14:59,765 --> 00:15:00,633
Eat up.

402
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:05,170
WIFE FIRST WHEN IT COMES TO DUMPLINGS

403
00:15:06,038 --> 00:15:07,139
Come on.

404
00:15:07,206 --> 00:15:09,608
I think these are short rib dumplings.

405
00:15:10,309 --> 00:15:11,510
Sounds good.

406
00:15:12,945 --> 00:15:14,046
Oh, it's tofu.

407
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:18,250
TOFU

408
00:15:18,317 --> 00:15:20,619
I thought of something else
we shouldn't do.

409
00:15:20,686 --> 00:15:21,654
What?

410
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:22,788
If you don't know,

411
00:15:23,489 --> 00:15:25,157
you don't have to act like you know.

412
00:15:25,891 --> 00:15:26,992
I'm just making an effort.

413
00:15:27,059 --> 00:15:28,360
I'm giving it a guess.

414
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:31,063
Oh, she meant they'll be serving
the short rib dumplings next.

415
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,703
FLINCH

416
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:39,138
-Is it good?
-Yes.

417
00:15:39,204 --> 00:15:40,039
That's a relief.

418
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:41,507
I'll pour you a glass.

419
00:15:42,007 --> 00:15:43,142
This is meat.

420
00:15:43,842 --> 00:15:47,146
-So one was…
-One was tofu, and the other was meat.

421
00:15:47,746 --> 00:15:50,616
SHORT RIB DUMPLING

422
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:55,621
-How is it?
-Good.

423
00:15:59,224 --> 00:16:00,793
NOD OF APPROVAL

424
00:16:04,263 --> 00:16:06,498
The texture is almost like…

425
00:16:06,565 --> 00:16:07,833
Like what?

426
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:12,604
WHAT DOES DO-YEON THINK
OF THE MAJIANG LIANGPI'S MOUTHFEEL?

427
00:16:12,671 --> 00:16:13,839
It feels like a tongue.

428
00:16:16,508 --> 00:16:17,509
What do you mean?

429
00:16:17,576 --> 00:16:18,877
I have no clue.

430
00:16:19,411 --> 00:16:20,980
It's super soft.

431
00:16:21,046 --> 00:16:22,181
It's a little…

432
00:16:22,247 --> 00:16:24,049
-The texture is…
-I'm not quite sure.

433
00:16:24,683 --> 00:16:26,952
It felt like
I was eating something sacred.

434
00:16:27,019 --> 00:16:29,655
You really have a way with words.

435
00:16:29,722 --> 00:16:33,792
I also kept thinking,
"Why does it feel like I'm kissing?"

436
00:16:33,859 --> 00:16:36,562
Why does it keep
wrapping around my tongue?

437
00:16:36,628 --> 00:16:37,930
It's caressing my tongue.

438
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:44,036
ENTER MORE DUMPLINGS

439
00:16:44,103 --> 00:16:46,372
Is there anywhere you've wanted to visit?

440
00:16:46,438 --> 00:16:47,706
-There is.
-Where?

441
00:16:47,773 --> 00:16:49,408
The places I used to go to

442
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:51,010
when I was living here.

443
00:16:51,076 --> 00:16:53,445
Places I went on memorable occasions.

444
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:54,613
On my birthday,

445
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:57,983
when my friends took me out to celebrate.

446
00:16:58,050 --> 00:17:00,419
There's a place called Central Street.

447
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:01,687
-Central Street?
-Yes.

448
00:17:01,754 --> 00:17:03,922
What happens there?
I've heard a lot about it.

449
00:17:03,989 --> 00:17:06,592
There are a lot of trendy shops there.

450
00:17:07,493 --> 00:17:10,996
The night lights are pretty,
and the architecture too.

451
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:12,765
-It's pretty?
-Yes.

452
00:17:12,831 --> 00:17:15,434
There are a lot of great buildings
with Eastern European influence.

453
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:17,369
I've wanted to go back.

454
00:17:17,436 --> 00:17:18,303
To Central Street?

455
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:21,740
I was feeling so lonely on my birthday,
but my friends cheered me up there.

456
00:17:22,241 --> 00:17:24,943
I pretended to be surprised
and shed a few tears.

457
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:26,745
I said, "What did you prepare
all this for?"

458
00:17:26,812 --> 00:17:28,247
-Because you were grateful?
-Yes.

459
00:17:28,313 --> 00:17:29,448
How old were you back then?

460
00:17:30,015 --> 00:17:31,116
Around 20 or so?

461
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,919
-You were just a baby.
-Twenty or twenty-one.

462
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:37,089
This all feels so good, honestly.

463
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:39,691
Back at the airport,
I couldn't quite believe it.

464
00:17:39,758 --> 00:17:41,193
It is a little bizarre, right?

465
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,695
It doesn't quite make sense to me.

466
00:17:43,762 --> 00:17:45,664
The whole thing feels surreal.

467
00:17:46,198 --> 00:17:49,334
I'd vaguely thought about
returning here with my future wife,

468
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,770
but I never imagined I'd be here with you.

469
00:17:52,471 --> 00:17:53,372
And I never imagined

470
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:56,075
that you would get whisked away
for a Covid test.

471
00:17:56,141 --> 00:17:57,276
WHAT'S THIS ABOUT…?

472
00:17:57,342 --> 00:17:58,610
As soon as we got on the plane,

473
00:17:58,677 --> 00:18:00,446
I completely crashed.

474
00:18:00,512 --> 00:18:01,480
And once we landed,

475
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,649
the lady made such a charismatic entrance.

476
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:05,717
-She did.
-To do Covid tests.

477
00:18:06,518 --> 00:18:08,153
As if to say, "You're all screwed."

478
00:18:09,888 --> 00:18:12,091
It did feel as though
they were going to lock the doors.

479
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:14,493
The stewardesses drew the curtains,

480
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,427
so I thought,

481
00:18:17,329 --> 00:18:18,664
"This has nothing to do with us."

482
00:18:18,730 --> 00:18:20,699
Then suddenly, Do-yeon took off.

483
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:23,168
They suddenly called "Jang Do-yeon."
So I said, "That's me."

484
00:18:25,337 --> 00:18:27,940
Harbin chose you, I guess.

485
00:18:29,074 --> 00:18:32,111
You didn't speak any Mandarin
when you first came to study, right?

486
00:18:32,177 --> 00:18:33,579
No, I came prepared.

487
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,449
That's it for the Mandarin talk.

488
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:41,386
I wanted to get some juicy details
about your hardships,

489
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:43,322
but let's move on to the next chapter.

490
00:18:43,822 --> 00:18:45,924
Was it hard making friends at all?

491
00:18:45,991 --> 00:18:47,226
Not hard, per se.

492
00:18:47,726 --> 00:18:48,594
I think I…

493
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:50,662
That's all for the friend talk.

494
00:18:51,163 --> 00:18:52,931
-Now, the next chapter.
-I mean, sure.

495
00:18:53,432 --> 00:18:56,535
It was a definite adjustment to be abroad,

496
00:18:56,602 --> 00:18:58,470
but I never felt particularly alone.

497
00:18:58,537 --> 00:19:00,405
Were you dating a fellow student?

498
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:01,306
I dated, yes.

499
00:19:01,373 --> 00:19:02,908
-You loved?
-Yes.

500
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:04,676
She was from Russia.

501
00:19:05,911 --> 00:19:06,778
That's awesome.

502
00:19:06,845 --> 00:19:08,814
-Was she also a student?
-Yes.

503
00:19:09,548 --> 00:19:10,883
We dated in secret.

504
00:19:10,949 --> 00:19:12,084
Why in secret?

505
00:19:12,584 --> 00:19:15,654
I felt a little shy about dating,

506
00:19:15,721 --> 00:19:19,424
so we would secretly meet at night,
after class, on the 16th floor.

507
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:20,659
What was on the 16th floor?

508
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,695
There were these researchers' labs.

509
00:19:23,762 --> 00:19:26,298
I'm not saying we went in there.
We hung out on the stairs.

510
00:19:26,365 --> 00:19:27,199
You did?

511
00:19:27,266 --> 00:19:28,400
"How was today?"

512
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:29,868
"That's what you got up to?"

513
00:19:30,369 --> 00:19:34,273
I would teach her Korean,
and she taught me some Russian.

514
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,841
Are you okay to talk about this?

515
00:19:35,908 --> 00:19:37,643
This was almost 20 years ago,

516
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:40,045
and I'm married now, so…

517
00:19:40,579 --> 00:19:42,014
MARRIED FOR AN HOUR

518
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:42,948
One glass, please.

519
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:45,617
BOWS IN SHAME

520
00:19:46,118 --> 00:19:49,054
Why are you opening
the Pandora's box of my past?

521
00:19:50,055 --> 00:19:51,957
So you dated a Russian woman, did you?

522
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:56,028
What matters is who I'm here with now.

523
00:19:56,728 --> 00:19:57,563
That would be me.

524
00:19:57,629 --> 00:19:59,031
That's what's important.

525
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:01,800
Let's not dwell on the past.
Just look straight ahead.

526
00:20:02,301 --> 00:20:03,402
We have two days left.

527
